{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25599696",
      "title": "Adding a First Class-based Component",
      "sourceHash": "1b13312d8d94cdf35a995377eac4fa90179a5302cadcb56932b64f9e9c1219dc",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.2,
          "end": 5.2,
          "en": "Now to dive into class-based components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.2,
          "end": 8.28,
          "en": "I got another starting project for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.28,
          "end": 11.36,
          "en": "And you'll find it attached to this lecture of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.36,
          "end": 15.18,
          "en": "Simply download it, extract it, run npn install,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.18,
          "end": 16.96,
          "en": "and then npn start,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.96,
          "end": 20.693,
          "en": "and you will see this simple demo app here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.57,
          "end": 22.94,
          "en": "Here we've got a button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.94,
          "end": 25.683,
          "en": "where we can toggle this list of users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.67,
          "end": 28.53,
          "en": "Now that's all not too fancy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.53,
          "end": 30.9,
          "en": "And it's simply built by, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.9,
          "end": 34.24,
          "en": "using two components and the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.24,
          "end": 37.78,
          "en": "We've got the users component with some dummy users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.78,
          "end": 40.94,
          "en": "And there we got the toggle user handler function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.94,
          "end": 42.29,
          "en": "And then in the end here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.29,
          "end": 45.3,
          "en": "we simply create our list of users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.3,
          "end": 47.78,
          "en": "by replicating the user component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.78,
          "end": 50.41,
          "en": "And we got a button which triggers that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.41,
          "end": 53.32,
          "en": "which changes the state with user state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.32,
          "end": 58.32,
          "en": "which controls whether that users list is visible or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.46,
          "end": 60.72,
          "en": "And inside the user component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.72,
          "end": 64.24,
          "en": "I simply render a list item with some styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.24,
          "end": 65.763,
          "en": "and I'm using props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.72,
          "end": 68.75,
          "en": "So that's all not too fancy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.75,
          "end": 69.583,
          "en": "And that's of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.583,
          "end": 73.42,
          "en": "all something you learn throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.42,
          "end": 75.91,
          "en": "Now let's learn how we could write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.91,
          "end": 80.23,
          "en": "this user component as a class-based component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.23,
          "end": 84.73,
          "en": "So how we can transform this to a class-based component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.73,
          "end": 88.74,
          "en": "And for this, we start with the class keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.74,
          "end": 89.57300000000001,
          "en": "Which again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.57300000000001,
          "end": 93.9,
          "en": "just to make this really clear is built into JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.9,
          "end": 95.91,
          "en": "It's not a React concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.91,
          "end": 100.4,
          "en": "Modern JavaScript supports classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.4,
          "end": 103.55,
          "en": "Now here, we would define a class named user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.55,
          "end": 106.4,
          "en": "And when we define a class in Java script,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.4,
          "end": 107.75,
          "en": "it looks like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.75,
          "end": 110.12,
          "en": "class, then the name of the class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.12,
          "end": 114.173,
          "en": "and then curly braces in which we define the class now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.3,
          "end": 118.07,
          "en": "And inside of these curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.07,
          "end": 121.82,
          "en": "we can now start adding methods to this class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.82,
          "end": 124.61,
          "en": "And for example, we can add a constructor method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.61,
          "end": 127.63,
          "en": "Here, we could do some initialization work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.63,
          "end": 129.61,
          "en": "and I'll come back to this in a second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.61,
          "end": 132.95,
          "en": "but actually I got no initialization work in this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.95,
          "end": 136.57,
          "en": "So I will just remove the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.57,
          "end": 139.223,
          "en": "Instead, we should add a render method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.15,
          "end": 141.6,
          "en": "Now, theoretically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.6,
          "end": 145.51,
          "en": "we can add as many methods as we want to a class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.51,
          "end": 147.633,
          "en": "and we can name them however we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.54,
          "end": 153.54,
          "en": "Render just is a specific method expected by React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.62,
          "end": 158.1,
          "en": "which React will call when it finds a component being used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.1,
          "end": 159.41,
          "en": "in JS X code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.41,
          "end": 161.57,
          "en": "Like we're doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.57,
          "end": 164.59,
          "en": "And then React will call the render method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.59,
          "end": 168.15,
          "en": "to find out what should be rendered to the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.15,
          "end": 170.84,
          "en": "So the render method in a clause in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.84,
          "end": 173.96,
          "en": "is your equivalent to your return statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.96,
          "end": 177.09,
          "en": "in a functional component, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.09,
          "end": 178.41,
          "en": "And in the render method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.41,
          "end": 181.44,
          "en": "you then also need to return the result,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.44,
          "end": 182.923,
          "en": "that should be rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.01,
          "end": 187.06,
          "en": "So that's now how we can rebuild this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.06,
          "end": 189.98,
          "en": "Though, one important thing is missing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 189.98,
          "end": 191.96,
          "en": "And that would be the props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 191.96,
          "end": 194.42,
          "en": "In the function component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 194.42,
          "end": 197.65,
          "en": "we receive props as a parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 197.65,
          "end": 201.2,
          "en": "Automatically passed in by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 201.2,
          "end": 204.89,
          "en": "In the class based component, that's not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 204.89,
          "end": 209.2,
          "en": "Here, the render method does not receive props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 209.2,
          "end": 212.09,
          "en": "Instead though we need to do something else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 212.09,
          "end": 213.91,
          "en": "Not just for props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 213.91,
          "end": 217.888,
          "en": "but to make the class based component work in general.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 217.888,
          "end": 222.77,
          "en": "We need to import component from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 224.9,
          "end": 229.06,
          "en": "And then we need to extend component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 229.06,
          "end": 233.18,
          "en": "which is also a built in concept in modern Java script.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 233.18,
          "end": 237.19,
          "en": "You can build classes which extend other classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.19,
          "end": 240.52,
          "en": "So which inherit from other classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.52,
          "end": 243.51,
          "en": "And now our custom user class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 243.51,
          "end": 246.49,
          "en": "inherits from the component class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 246.49,
          "end": 248.57,
          "en": "which is defined by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 248.57,
          "end": 251.3,
          "en": "Now this component class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 251.3,
          "end": 253.41,
          "en": "adds important functionality,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 253.41,
          "end": 256.31,
          "en": "to make your class work as a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 256.31,
          "end": 258.75,
          "en": "And that's the important part for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 258.75,
          "end": 263.73,
          "en": "Now, it also adds a couple of important properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 263.73,
          "end": 266.67,
          "en": "For example, the props property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 266.67,
          "end": 270.113,
          "en": "which we can now access with this props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 271.15,
          "end": 274.25,
          "en": "This is only possible because we extend component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 274.25,
          "end": 275.17,
          "en": "Because of that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 275.17,
          "end": 278.52,
          "en": "there will be a props property in our clause",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 278.52,
          "end": 281.97,
          "en": "which we can access through this keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 281.97,
          "end": 284.79,
          "en": "And that contains all the props data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 284.79,
          "end": 288.02,
          "en": "we received for our component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 288.02,
          "end": 291.11,
          "en": "And now we've got the class-based equivalent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 291.11,
          "end": 293.25,
          "en": "to our functional component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 293.25,
          "end": 296.053,
          "en": "which we can now remove or comment out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 297,
          "end": 298.26,
          "en": "And I'll do the latter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 298.26,
          "end": 302.82,
          "en": "so that we still see both in side by side comparison.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 302.82,
          "end": 303.653,
          "en": "As you can tell,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 303.653,
          "end": 306.4,
          "en": "the functional component is a bit leaner,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 306.4,
          "end": 310.73,
          "en": "which is one of the main reasons why they are more popular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 310.73,
          "end": 313.7,
          "en": "But other than that it is the same now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 313.7,
          "end": 317.902,
          "en": "We also still export user and now we can save this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 317.902,
          "end": 321.33,
          "en": "And if I reload, we get the same app as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 321.33,
          "end": 324.38,
          "en": "and it works and looks like before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 324.38,
          "end": 328.02,
          "en": "And that is also a very important takeaway here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 328.02,
          "end": 331.37,
          "en": "Class-based components can work together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 331.37,
          "end": 334.15999999999997,
          "en": "with functional components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 334.15999999999997,
          "end": 339.15999999999997,
          "en": "Users is a functional component, but it renders user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 339.209,
          "end": 341.89,
          "en": "which is a class-based component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 341.89,
          "end": 344.47,
          "en": "And that is absolutely no problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 344.47,
          "end": 347.34000000000003,
          "en": "A class-based component could also render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 347.34000000000003,
          "end": 350.9,
          "en": "a functional component that would also work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 350.9,
          "end": 353.28,
          "en": "In the end, these are just components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 353.28,
          "end": 356.47,
          "en": "and you can mix and match them as you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 356.47,
          "end": 361.09,
          "en": "In reality, you will most likely build a project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 361.09,
          "end": 364.32,
          "en": "by either sticking to just functional",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 364.32,
          "end": 367.67,
          "en": "or to just class-based components though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 367.67,
          "end": 371.48,
          "en": "You can mix and match, but that will mostly matter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 371.48,
          "end": 374.91,
          "en": "if you are working on an existing application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 374.91,
          "end": 376.97,
          "en": "and you're adding new features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 376.97,
          "end": 380.04,
          "en": "and you may be also step by step migrate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 380.04,
          "end": 382.82,
          "en": "from class-based to functional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 382.82,
          "end": 385.42,
          "en": "If you're starting a brand new project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 385.42,
          "end": 388.47,
          "en": "you will probably go with your favorite approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 388.47,
          "end": 390.81,
          "en": "whatever that is and then stick to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 390.81,
          "end": 393.43,
          "en": "But you can mix and match it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 393.43,
          "end": 396.93,
          "en": "And that is how you build class-based components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 396.93,
          "end": 399.04,
          "en": "Now, however, I did mention that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 399.04,
          "end": 401.68,
          "en": "we had to use them in the past,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 401.68,
          "end": 403.94,
          "en": "when it came to managing state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 403.94,
          "end": 407.42,
          "en": "like we're doing it here in the user's JS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 407.42,
          "end": 410.76,
          "en": "Therefore let's find out how that works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 410.76,
          "end": 412.823,
          "en": "with class-based components now.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}